# PLAN reference: "TLS: Caddy + Let's Encrypt via DNS-01... for a subdomain
# of a domain the parent owns... No internal CA to distribute, automatic
# renewal, and it works identically from the parent's phone on cellular if
# they later expose it via Tailscale/WireGuard."
#
# Set HUB_DOMAIN in deploy/.env to your real subdomain (e.g.
# hub.yourfamily.example) to get automatic HTTPS via DNS-01 -- fill in your
# DNS provider's plugin/API token per https://caddyserver.com/docs/caddyfile/directives/tls
# (the exact directive depends on which DNS provider you use; Caddy's default
# build only supports HTTP-01/TLS-ALPN, so a DNS-01 setup needs a
# provider-specific Caddy build -- xcaddy or a prebuilt image with the plugin).
#
# For a pure-LAN deployment with no public DNS, use a bare :80 site instead
# (see the commented block below) and reach the hub only over your own
# network or a WireGuard/Tailscale tunnel -- never expose plain HTTP to the
# internet.

#{$HUB_DOMAIN:localhost} {
#	reverse_proxy hub:8000
#}

# --- LAN-only alternative (no public DNS, no TLS) ---
:80 {	
  reverse_proxy hub:8000
}
